Virtual Hospital System
1. Project Overview

The Virtual Hospital System is a comprehensive healthcare platform designed to simplify and enhance access to medical services. It provides users with the ability to:

Book hospital visits and doctor appointments.

Purchase medicines online.

Access information about nearby blood banks, sperm banks, and the latest medical facilities.

Use an emergency chatbot for real-time assistance based on reported symptoms, which suggests medicines and recommends hospitals.

This system integrates frontend and backend functionality to provide a seamless user experience for both regular and emergency healthcare needs.

2. Key Features

User Account Management – Register, login, and manage personal profile.

Appointment Booking – Schedule visits with hospitals and doctors.

Medicine Purchase – Search, order, and track medicines online.

Nearby Health Resources – Locate blood banks, sperm banks, and hospitals.

Emergency Chatbot – Rule based symptom checker for immediate advice and hospital recommendations.

Notifications – Alerts for appointments, medicine deliveries, and emergency suggestions.

3. Tech Stack

Frontend: TypeScript + Vite + TailwindCSS

Backend: Node.js + Express

Database: SQL (configured with Drizzle ORM)

Other Libraries: Chatbot APIs, Payment Gateway (if integrated), utility libraries in shared folder

Build Tools: Vite for frontend bundling

Styling: TailwindCSS

4. Folder Structure
/virtual-hospital
│
├── backend/             # Backend APIs and server-side logic
├── client/              # Frontend application (UI, pages, components)
├── server/              # Main server setup and entry point
├── shared/              # Shared types, interfaces, and utilities
├── script/              # Automation scripts and helpers
├── node_modules/        # Installed npm dependencies
├── package.json         # Project dependencies and scripts
├── package-lock.json    # Exact versions of installed dependencies
├── tsconfig.json        # TypeScript configuration
├── tailwind.config.ts   # TailwindCSS configuration
├── postcss.config.js    # PostCSS setup
├── vite.config.ts       # Vite build configuration
├── drizzle.config.ts    # Drizzle ORM configuration for database
├── components.json      # UI components metadata/configuration


Explanation of folders:

backend/ – Contains all REST API routes and business logic for appointments, medicines, and emergency features.

client/ – Frontend app, including pages, components, and styling. Handles user interaction.

server/ – Starts the server and connects backend APIs with frontend.

shared/ – Contains reusable types, schemas, and utility functions for both frontend and backend.

script/ – Automation scripts, database seeding, or maintenance tasks.

5. Installation & Setup

Step 1: Clone the repository

git clone <your-repo-link>


Step 2: Install dependencies

npm install


Step 3: Run the project

Backend & Server

npm run dev


Frontend

npm run client


Step 4: Environment variables

Configure .env file for database, API keys, and other secrets as per drizzle.config.ts.

6. Usage

Open the frontend in a browser.

Sign up or log in with your account.

Navigate through pages to:

Book appointments with doctors.

Purchase medicines online.

Locate nearby blood banks, sperm banks, and hospitals.

Access the Emergency Section to interact with the chatbot for symptom-based suggestions.

Follow notifications for appointments or medicine deliveries.

